    "title": "J. Cole's 'The Fall-Off': A track-by-track guide to his final album",
    "text": "LOCALJ. Cole's 'The Fall-Off' is a 10-year journey back to his Fayetteville rootsRakeem \"Keem\" JonesCorrespondentFeb. 18, 2026, 5:04 a.m. ETJ. Cole’s latest project, \"The Fall-Off,\" is an “if you know, you know” album. The 24-track project is a collection of stories from in and around Fayetteville.From the beginning to the end, the Terry Sanford graduate displays his pride for the All-American city. Rather than present a false image of himself and his home city, he highlights the beauty of the struggle. This project is for the underserved, underrepresented and unheard section of Fayetteville that encompasses areas like Bonnie Doone, Shaw Road, Moore Street and Murchison Road.",
